  "source": "simulator_check/cases/variables_with_several_values.json",
  "question": "What does AWS do with a policy variable whose key has several values? AWS says \"You can't use a multivalued condition key as a variable\", but not what happens if a policy does. The analyzer refuses.",
  "description": "Third follow-up: a Deny with StringNotEquals s3:prefix ${aws:TagKeys}, under an Allow for all of S3, listing the prefix red, the second value.",
  "readings": {
    "EXPLICIT_DENY": "the variable matches nothing, so StringNotEquals holds, as AWS documents for a variable with no value; or only blue is used",
    "ALLOW": "a value of the key is used, so red matches; or the statement is dropped"
  },
